        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Word of Honor (2003 film)\n- People: Don Johnson, Jeanne Tripplehorn, Sharon Lawrence, John Heard, Arliss Howard, Robert Markowitz\n- Roles: actor, producer, director, singer, songwriter\n- Awards: Golden Globe, Hollywood Walk of Fame, Offshore World Cup\n- Systems: Miami Vice, Nash Bridges\n\nFacts:\n- Don Johnson was born on December 15, 1949.\n- Don Johnson is an American actor, producer, director, singer, and songwriter.\n- Don Johnson played James \"Sonny\" Crockett in the 1980s television series Miami Vice.\n- Don Johnson had the lead role in the 1990s cop series Nash Bridges.\n- Don Johnson won a Golden Globe for Miami Vice.\n- Don Johnson was the American Power Boat Association's 1988 World Champion of the Offshore World Cup.\n- Don Johnson received a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame.\n- Robert Markowitz directed television films including Decoration Day in 1990, Because Mommy Works in 1994, The Tuskegee Airmen in 1995, The Great Gatsby in 2000, The Pilot's Wife in 2003, Word of Honor in 2003, and Avenger in 2006.\n- Word of Honor is an American television film released in 2003.\n- Word of Honor stars Don Johnson, Jeanne Tripplehorn, Sharon Lawrence, John Heard, and Arliss Howard.",
